@H 1121 := "phi-signsplit-opponent — does faithful↑/big-Φ↓ split appear on the anima ENGINE-A⊥G opponent substrate, or is it planning-specific?" :: discovery [closed]
  seed = "the H_1059–1066 planning Φ-measure-dependence arc (faithful φ_EI↑ / big-Φ↓ sign-split) was measured on a PLANNING toy substrate; H_1062 showed the split's clean ZCA-removable CAUSAL mechanism is planning-bounded. THIS asks whether the SAME sign-split recurs when the n≤5 channel substrate is driven by the anima engine's A⊥G OPPONENT dynamics (per-channel out = engine_A(x)−engine_G(x), the H404 dual-FFN repulsion form) instead of planning — is the split an A⊥G-opponent-composition property or planning-specific?"
